WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.773
Book 13's loop has five
steps: test, detect drift,

2
00:00:03.773 --> 00:00:07.888
raise a typed task, actuate,
and close with evidence.

3
00:00:07.888 --> 00:00:11.700
Here, SailPoint and the kit's
reconciliation do the testing.

4
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:14.338
SailPoint's change events detect drift.

5
00:00:14.338 --> 00:00:18.263
A SailPoint workflow posting
to ServiceNow raises the task.

6
00:00:18.263 --> 00:00:22.350
SailPoint's connectors, and
ServiceNow's Entra spoke, actuate.

7
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.937
And a re-read closes the
loop, not the ticket status.

8
00:00:25.937 --> 00:00:30.250
Used as shipped, the products fall
short of the loop in four places.

9
00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.050
First, a ticket status isn't a re-read.

10
00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:36.725
SailPoint treats a mapped
ServiceNow status as complete.

11
00:00:36.725 --> 00:00:41.188
Second, the catalog app moves
access approval into ServiceNow.

12
00:00:41.188 --> 00:00:46.050
Third, SailPoint's service desk
integration can't raise change requests.

13
00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:48.943
And fourth, there are two
doors into the directory,

14
00:00:48.943 --> 00:00:52.825
because SailPoint and Entra inbound
provisioning can both write.

15
00:00:52.825 --> 00:00:55.460
Each gap is closed by a specific gate.
